1. Job and JobRepository – How Spring Batch manages job executions.
2. JobOperator – How jobs are launched programmatically.
3. Tasklet processing – How a single task is executed.
4. Chunk processing – Reader → Processor → Writer.
5. JobParameters – How Spring Batch identifies individual job executions.
6. JobExecution and StepExecution – How execution status and metadata are maintained.
One particularly important distinction to understand is why 
we use different JobParameters for different executions.